              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coalgebra"} most familiar sense
            %em coalgebra
            is just like an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-monoid"} co-monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            equipped with a multiplication
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  m \colon A \otimes A \to A
          %p and a unit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i \colon k \to A
          %p
            satisfying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
            law and left/right
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+laws"} unit laws
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+diagrams"} commutative diagrams
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"}> Dually
            , a
            %strong coalgebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a vector space equipped with a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comultiplication"} comultiplication
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta \colon C \to C \otimes C
          %p
            and a
            %strong counit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e \colon C \to k
          %p
            satisfying
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-associativity"} co-associativity
            and left/right
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-unitality"} co-unitality
            laws.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+diagrams"} commutative diagrams
            for these laws are obtained by taking the diagrams for the associative and left/right unit laws and turning all the arrows around.
          %p
            %img{:alt => "axioms", :src => "http://presheaf.com/cache/d1n601e593w4j122e1nrx3j1d3v68b.png"}/
          %p
            We can express this idea much more efficiently using the concept of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
            %strong coalgebra
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} in
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect^{op}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect
          %p
            Coalgebras of this sort are an important ingredient in more sophisticated structures such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bialgebra"} bialgebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebras
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+algebra"} Frobenius algebras
          %p More generally:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra+for+an+endofunctor"} coalgebra for an endofunctor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to C
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                – an
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  \-coalgebra
                – is
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    of
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi C
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %li
                  %p
                    and a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                            %mo :
                            %mi A
                            %mo →
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : A \to F(A)
            %li
              %p
                a general
                %strong coassociative coalgebra
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra+over+a+comonad"} coalgebra over a comonad
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebra over a monad
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#special_cases Special cases
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                a commutative ring, if the endofunction
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to C
                is
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : R Mod \to R Mod
                given by
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo :
                        %mi N
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi N
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : N \mapsto N \otimes N
                = succeed "-coalgebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %msup
                          %mi Mod
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod^{op}
                = succeed "\u2018s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"} Tom Leinster
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/12/the_status_of_coalgebra.html#c020741"} here
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity-algebra"}> algebra
                s are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CoDGCA"} cocommutative comonoids
                in the category of chain complexes.
          %h3#classes_with_extra_properties_and_structure Classes with extra properties and structure
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+coalgebra"}> Banach coalgebra
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+coalgebra"} C-star coalgebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+coalgebra"} measure coalgebra
          %h3#other Other
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dyadic+interval+coalgebra"} dyadic interval coalgebra
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decimal+interval+coalgebra"} decimal interval coalgebra
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+interval+coalgebra"} rational interval coalgebra
          %h2#differential_graded_coalgebras Differential graded coalgebras
          %p
            These are explored briefly in the lexicon style entry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+coalgebra"} differential graded coalgebra
          %h2#cocommutative_coassociative_coalgebras Cocommutative coassociative coalgebras
          %p
            These, in most cases, form a complete cocomplete Cartesian Closed Category,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Coalg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Coalg
            over which the category,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-coalgebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-dimension" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_f
            the category of (commutative associative) algebras that are finite.
          %p
            The basic fact is that a coalgebra is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
            of its finite dimensional subcoalgebras. It follows from this that we can identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Coalg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Coalg
            with the category of finite-limit-preserving
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            its
            = succeed "-vector-space" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
            is a finite coalgebra.
          %p
            The product of coalgebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
