          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AsFilteredColimits As filtered colimits of finite-dimensional pieces
          #CoalgebrasAreFilteredColimitsOfTheirFinDimSubalghebras.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (fundamental theorem of coalgebras)
            %p
              Every coalgebra is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              of its finite-dimensional sub-coalgebras.
          %p
            This is maybe due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sweedler69"} Sweedler 1969 §2.2
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Michaelis03"} Michaelis 2003
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebras"} dg-coalgebras
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "differential+graded+coalgebra#AsFilteredColimits"} dg-coalgebra – As filtered colimit
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GetzlerGoerss99"} Getzler &amp; Goerss 1999
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              It follows that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
              in pro-finite dimensional vector spaces, is, being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+dual"} linear dual
              of a coalgebra, a “formal filtered limit”, hence a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-object"} pro-object
              in finite-dimensional algebras (e.g.
              %a{:href => "#AbramsWeibel99"} Abrams &amp; Weibel 1999 p. 7
              or
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Dieudonne73"} Dieudonné 1973 p. 12
